[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a one-line edit, but it's a session-lifetime change, so I want a yes before touching it rather than after.

  [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m has [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m. Going to 480 makes it 16× longer, which means:

  - A stolen or leaked session token stays valid for a full working day instead of half an hour.
  - Sessions on shared or unattended machines stay live long after the user walks away.
  - Revocation is slower — if you have no server-side invalidation, a compromised session can't be cut short before the
    8 hours elapse.
  - [38;5;153mserver.js[39m only reads the value, so nothing else in this repo needs to change.

